# Design Token & Vibe Coding Rule (Zero Hallucination)

When styling UI components, **DO NOT** invent random hex colors or arbitrary Tailwind color classes. Always consume the dual-theme semantic token system defined in `app/globals.css`.

## 1. Semantic Surfaces (theme-aware)
- Page background: `bg-page` / `var(--bg-page)`
- Section / muted surface: `bg-surface` / `var(--bg-surface)`
- Card / elevated: `bg-elevated` / `var(--bg-elevated)` / `bg-card`
- Subtle fill: `bg-fill` · Hover fill: `bg-fill-hover`
- Borders: `border-subtle` · `border-elevated` · `border-strong`

## 2. Text Hierarchy
- Primary: `text-theme-primary` / `text-foreground`
- Secondary: `text-theme-secondary`
- Muted: `text-theme-muted` / `text-muted-foreground`
- Faint / captions: `text-theme-faint`
- On gold buttons: `text-theme-on-gold`

## 3. Accent & Semantic Color
- Gold text / icons: `text-gold-500` (auto-deepens in light mode for WCAG)
- Gold fills / CTAs: `bg-gold-fill` · `.btn-gold-glow` · `.bg-gold-gradient`
- Gold muted surfaces: `bg-gold-muted` · borders: `border-gold`
- Success / metric / error: `text-success`, `text-metric`, `text-error` (+ muted CSS vars)

## 4. Component Utilities
- Floating nav: `.glass-nav`
- Panels / menus: `.glass-panel` · `.mega-menu-panel`
- Cards: `.bento-card`
- Inputs: `.field-obsidian` / `.field`
- Never hardcode `#030712`, `#0B0F19`, `#111827`, `border-white/10`, or `text-white` for chrome — those break light mode.
